[size=4][b]Your character turns to face the direction it is actually moving.[/b][/size]

In the base game the body stays locked to the camera, so moving backwards or sideways plays a backpedal or a strafe. This mod turns the character to face its movement direction so it simply runs, the way most third person action games handle it.

The camera is untouched. You still aim it freely, and the character follows where you are going.

[b]Work in progress.[/b] This is an early release. It is stable and playable, but a few rough edges remain and are being worked on. Feedback and reports are welcome.


[size=4][b]Where it acts[/b][/size]

Walking, jogging and jumping, with the weapon put away.

Sprinting, climbing a ladder, zero g, sitting and holding a weapon are left alone: in those situations the character behaves exactly as it would without the mod installed. That is deliberate, and it is what fixes the ladder and zero g reports from the previous version.

[b]F11[/b] switches the mod off and back on without leaving the game, for anything still misbehaving. To move the shortcut elsewhere, put a virtual key code in [b]Documents/My Games/Starfield/SFSE/sf360.ini[/b], the same folder the log is written to. [b]0[/b] removes it.

[code]toggleKey=122[/code]

Turning is still abrupt, most noticeably with keyboard and mouse. That is the next thing being worked on.


[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Starfield 1.16.244
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/106]SFSE[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/3256]Address Library for SFSE Plugins[/url]
[/list]


[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Install with a mod manager, or unpack into your Starfield [b]Data[/b] folder:

[code]Data/SFSE/Plugins/sf360.dll
Data/meshes/actors/human/animations/...[/code]

Loose files have to be enabled.

[b]Documents/My Games/Starfield/StarfieldCustom.ini[/b] needs:

[code][Archive]
bInvalidateOlderFiles=1
sResourceDataDirsFinal=[/code]


[size=4][b]About the included animation files[/b][/size]

The archive includes empty replacements for the movement start animations. Those animations carry root motion that fights the rotation, so blanking them removes a slide at the start of a movement. The visual cost is negligible, and they will be dropped once the interaction is fixed properly.


[size=4][b]Reporting a problem[/b][/size]

A log is written to [b]Documents/My Games/Starfield/SFSE/Logs/sf360.log[/b]. Please attach it to any bug report.


[size=4][b]Source[/b][/size]

The mod is open source: [url=https://github.com/rael-g/360DirectionalMovement]github.com/rael-g/360DirectionalMovement[/url]

